---
import Shrine from '../layouts/Shrine.astro';
---

<Shrine>
  <noscript>
    <p class="note">The shrine needs JavaScript to keep time with the server and to seal messages in your browser.</p>
  </noscript>

  <!-- The hero changes with the phase: a countdown while sealed, the opening ceremony on the Day. -->
  <section id="hero" class="hero center" data-phase="loading" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="eyebrow" id="hero-eyebrow">&nbsp;</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">The shrine</h1>

    <div id="ceremony" class="ceremony" hidden>
      <p class="eyebrow">The Number of <span data-year></span></p>
      <p class="number mono" id="number-dec" aria-label="The Number of the year">&nbsp;</p>
      <p class="number-hex mono" id="number-hex">&nbsp;</p>
      <div class="bit-row">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Bit</span>
        <span class="bit mono" id="bit">·</span>
      </div>
      <p class="dim small" id="ceremony-source">&nbsp;</p>
    </div>

    <div class="countdown mono" id="countdown" role="timer" aria-live="off">
      <div><span data-u="d">--</span><small>days</small></div>
      <div><span data-u="h">--</span><small>hours</small></div>
      <div><span data-u="m">--</span><small>minutes</small></div>
      <div><span data-u="s">--</span><small>seconds</small></div>
    </div>
    <p id="hero-sub" class="dim">&nbsp;</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="tower-panel" aria-labelledby="tower-h">
    <h2 id="tower-h"><span class="numeral">I</span>The Tower</h2>
    <p class="dim">
      Twelve rings, three pegs. Each Day the visitors vote and exactly one ring moves. When all twelve stand on C,
      programming is over. Played perfectly that takes 4,095 years: the year 6121 at the earliest.
    </p>
    <svg id="tower-svg" class="tower-svg"></svg>
    <p class="stat-row">
      <span>Moves made: <strong id="moves-made">–</strong>.</span>
      <span>Optimal moves remaining: <strong id="optimal-remaining">–</strong>.</span>
    </p>

    <div id="ballot" hidden>
      <hr class="thin" />
      <h3>The ballot of <span data-year></span></h3>
      <p class="dim">
        These are the only legal moves. Votes stay hidden until the window closes; then the move with the most votes
        is made. Nothing here tells you which move is wise. The crowd is on its own.
      </p>
      <div class="moves" id="moves" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Legal moves"></div>
      <div class="captcha" id="vote-captcha"></div>
      <p><button class="primary" id="vote-button" disabled>Cast your vote</button></p>
      <p id="vote-status" class="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
    <p><a href="/tower/">The full history of moves →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="guestbook-panel" aria-labelledby="gb-h">
    <h2 id="gb-h"><span class="numeral">II</span>The Sealed Guestbook</h2>
    <p class="dim">
      Each message is sealed in your browser inside a time-lock puzzle. Anyone can open it, but only by squaring a number
      over and over, trillions of times in a row. More computers do not help; only a faster one does. It is not
      quantum-safe: a large enough quantum computer would open every seal at once.
    </p>

    <div id="gb-closed">
      <p><strong id="gb-count">–</strong> <span id="gb-count-label">entries</span> sealed so far. The guestbook opens on the Day.</p>
    </div>

    <form id="gb-form" hidden>
      <label for="gb-text" class="eyebrow">Your message</label>
      <textarea id="gb-text" maxlength="4000" placeholder="To whoever opens this…"></textarea>
      <p class="counter mono small"><span id="gb-chars">0</span> / 1,000</p>

      <fieldset class="seals">
        <legend class="eyebrow">Choose a seal</legend>
        <label class="seal-option"><input type="radio" name="seal" value="short" checked /><span><strong>Short</strong><em>about 1 year</em><code data-t="short"></code></span></label>
        <label class="seal-option"><input type="radio" name="seal" value="decade" /><span><strong>Decade</strong><em>about 10 years</em><code data-t="decade"></code></span></label>
        <label class="seal-option"><input type="radio" name="seal" value="century" /><span><strong>Century</strong><em>about 100 years</em><code data-t="century"></code></span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <p class="small faint" id="gb-bench"></p>

      <p class="note">
        Nobody can read the entries, including us, so they cannot be moderated. Only ciphertext ever leaves your
        browser. One entry per person per year, up to 1,000 characters. Seals tend to fall early as computers get faster.
      </p>
      <div class="captcha" id="gb-captcha"></div>
      <p><button class="primary" id="gb-button" type="submit">Seal it</button></p>
      <ol class="steps small" id="gb-steps" hidden></ol>
      <p id="gb-status" class="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
    <p><a href="/archive/">The archive of sealed entries →</a> · <a href="/solver/">How to open one →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="number-panel" aria-labelledby="num-h">
    <h2 id="num-h"><span class="numeral">III</span>The Number and the Bit</h2>
    <p class="dim">
      Each Day has a random number and a random bit, taken from the drand beacon run by the League of Entropy. We do
      not choose them: the round that decides them is published a year in advance, and anyone can check it.
    </p>
    <div id="number-details"></div>
    <p><a href="/archive/">Every year's Number and Bit →</a></p>
  </section>
</Shrine>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 1rem 0 3.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
  }
  .countdown {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(0.7rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    margin: 0 auto 1.4rem;
  }
  .countdown div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    min-width: 3.2ch;
  }
  .countdown span {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 10vw, 4.4rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--gold-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    text-shadow: 0 0 28px rgba(220, 174, 85, 0.25);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .countdown small {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .hero[data-phase='open'] .countdown span {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 6vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-shadow: none;
  }
  .ceremony {
    margin: 0 auto 2.4rem;
  }
  .number {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 5.6vw, 2.5rem);
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--gold-2);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.2rem;
    text-shadow: 0 0 36px rgba(220, 174, 85, 0.35);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .number.drawing {
    color: var(--dim);
    text-shadow: none;
  }
  .number-hex {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .bit-row {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem 0.35rem 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .bit {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2.6rem;
    height: 2.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #4a3a1c, #1a140b);
    border: 1px solid #6d5428;
    color: var(--gold-2);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .tower-svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  hr.thin {
    margin: 1.8rem 0;
  }
  .moves {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .moves :global(button) {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.3rem;
  }
  .moves :global(button[aria-checked='true']) {
    border-color: var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold-2);
    background: #2a2010;
  }
  .status:empty {
    display: none;
  }
  .captcha:empty {
    display: none;
  }
  .captcha {
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .counter {
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin: 0.2rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .counter.over {
    color: #e08a6a;
  }
  .seals {
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  .seals legend {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .seal-option {
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .seal-option input {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
  }
  .seal-option span {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .seal-option em {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .seal-option code {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }
  .seal-option input:checked + span {
    border-color: var(--gold);
    background: #1f180d;
  }
  .seal-option input:focus-visible + span {
    outline: 2px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .steps {
    color: var(--dim);
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }
  .steps :global(li.done) {
    color: var(--ok);
  }
  .steps :global(li.active) {
    color: var(--gold-2);
  }
  #number-details :global(dl) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.2rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  #number-details :global(dt) {
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  #number-details :global(dd) {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    #number-details :global(dl) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }
    #number-details :global(dd) {
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { mountHome } from '../scripts/home';
  mountHome();
</script>
